<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-sordesco</span></b> , dŭi, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n., to
				become dirty, be soiled</i> (ante- and post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne coma fumo obsordescat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 214</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to wear out,
			decrease</i>: obsorduit jam haec in me aerumna, i. e. <i>is moderated</i>, Caecil. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 147, 7</span></i> (Com. Rel. v. 86
			Rib.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
